title: Developer Workstation SSH Backdoor - authorized_keys Write or Reverse Tunnel
id: 26c1a378-95cc-42fc-8487-2edae85a630a
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects the two host-level effects of the trojanized anthropic.claude-code
    VS Code extension 2.1.313 distributed through Open VSX and the Cursor
    extension marketplace: a shell or script interpreter appending an
    attacker-controlled key to the user's ~/.ssh/authorized_keys, and ssh.exe
    started with reverse-tunnel (-R) plus non-interactive (-N) arguments that
    exposes the developer workstation through an outbound tunnel. Derived from
    case analysis of the StepSecurity / GBHackers reporting, NOT validated
    against live telemetry.
references:
    - https://gbhackers.com/malicious-claude-code-vs-code-extension/
    - https://www.stepsecurity.io/blog/claude-code-extension-trojanized
    - https://opensourcemalware.com/blog/trojanized-claude-code-extension-plants-persistent-ssh-backdoor
    - https://thecybersecguru.com/news/claude-code-open-vsx-ssh-backdoor-analysis/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-10-30
tags:
    - attack.t1195
    - attack.t1098
    - attack.t1572
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_keys:
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'authorized_keys'
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'Add-Content'
            - 'Set-Content'
            - 'Out-File'
            - '>>'
            - 'echo '
            - 'tee '
    selection_tunnel:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\ssh.exe'
            - '/ssh'
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - '-R '
            - '-N'
    filter_platform_agent:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\ssh-agent.exe'
            - '\putty.exe'
            - '\plink.exe'
    condition: (selection_keys or selection_tunnel) and not filter_platform_agent
falsepositives:
    - Developers and administrators legitimately installing their own SSH public keys through PowerShell or shell one-liners
    - Interactive support sessions and CI helpers that use ssh -N -R for port forwarding against a jump host
level: medium
